  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Fair weather with day to day warming trend through \nSaturday.\n\nA broad area of surface high pressure is centered across the Corn \nBelt States this morning, and this feature will crest across our \nregion tonight. \n\nThis feature will maintain fair weather with clear skies through \nFriday, with a partly to mostly sunny sky Saturday as a little mid \nlevel moisture sneaks northward from OH/PA. \n\nDay to day warming will ensue as winds become southerly behind this \nsurface high. Highs in the 70s today will become highs in the 80s \nfor Saturday. Dewpoints, however, will remain relatively cool \nthrough Saturday, with values only nearing 60F, resulting in a not \nso humid airmass. \n\nThe light wind flow and clear skies will allow for radiational \nvalley fog, likely more extensive Thursday and Friday nights with a \nweaker wind flow at 1K feet.\n\n\nKey Message 2...Unsettled weather returns Sunday and into the \nbeginning of the new work week. \n\nSeveral convective shortwave troughs cresting a Rockies/Plains ridge \nof high pressure combined with the deepening upper level low near \nHudson Bay will return unsettled weather to our region by Sunday. \n\nSoutherly flow behind the recently departed surface high pressure \nsystem will advect deeper moisture (increasing humidity) across the \neastern Great Lakes with Pwat values reaching 1.5 inches or greater. \n\nModest instability across WNY will encourage convection through the \nday with scattered showers and thunderstorms developing, especially \nalong lake breeze boundaries. Additional shortwave troughs will \nmaintain showers and thunderstorms across our region Monday and into \nTuesday.",
